    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2YFH3nLwGkEpUY5fr2P61Pj)_\n\n**Before:** the Vulpea modules were spread over `libraries/modules/text/` (`base`, `ui`, `para`, `schemas`, `ext`, `ext-back`, `split`) and `funct/` (`convert-properties`, `grouped-backlinks`, `org-ql`), each with its own doc. `sp-vulpea-ext` also required `sp-vulpea-table`.\n\n**After:**\n- The ten modules moved (`git mv`) into `libraries/modules/vulpea/`, code unchanged, each still its own `.el` with its own `provide`. There is no loader module (an earlier version of this PR had `sp-vulpea`; removed as asked): `sp-org-ext` requires `sp-vulpea-base`, `-ui`, `-para`, `-schemas` and `-ext` itself, as before, and `-ext` still requires `-convert-properties`, `-grouped-backlinks` and `-split`.\n- Their ten docs are now one, `docs/tangles/vulpea/sp-vulpea.org`, with a section per file (same approach as #71): each section sets its target with a `:header-args:emacs-lisp+: :tangle ...` property. The old `sp-vulpea-split-old.org` note moved beside it.\n- `sp-vulpea-table` is excluded, as asked: the require is gone from `sp-vulpea-ext` (code and doc) and `sp-org-ext` requires it after the Vulpea modules.\n- `docs/main.org` gets a `vulpea/` section (links go to sections of the combined doc); `load-order.org` and its SVG (re-rendered with Graphviz), `conditional-loading.org` and the `sp-org-ext` doc follow. `tests/sp-vulpea-para-test.el` points at the new path. CHANGELOG has a \"Vulpea modules\" set.\n\n**Choices:** `sp-vulpea-ext-back` (an empty slot) and `sp-vulpea-org-ql` (a draft that runs a query at load) are moved and documented but not required by anything, as before; tangling gives `ext-back` its skeleton instead of an empty file. `sp-vulpea-grouped-backlinks` requires `sp-vulpea-table-core` (for the note selector), so Vulpea still pulls in that one table file.\n\n**Checked** (Emacs, container): tangling `sp-vulpea.org` gives the ten files identical to the old ones (apart from the `sp-vulpea-ext` change and the `ext-back` skeleton), parens check, and the 5 `sp-vulpea-para` ERT tests pass from the new path. **Not checked:** a real start with Elpaca and the vault.\n\n**Conflicts to expect:** #63 (defcustom group) and #66 (moves `load-order.org`) touch these files; #58 and #71 edit `docs/main.org`, `load-order.org` and the CHANGELOG nearby.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01HJHZkEqLs53FsVfwoPzyev",
